      en: {
        title:   "Artificial Intelligence & Big Data",
        excerpt: "How Jtech prevents errors and fraud.",
        content: "Artificial intelligence is revolutionizing the sanitation sector, especially in one of the most critical aspects of its operation: meter reading.\n\nSmall errors in this process can result in significant financial losses, damage customer relationships, and compromise the utility company's reputation.\n\nUsing advanced algorithms, the technology allows for the identification of errors and fraud in real time, ensuring greater accuracy, speed, and security in data collection.\n\nThis is precisely the path Jtech has been following by applying AI to the automation of meter reading reviews, an innovation that is transforming metering into an intelligent and reliable process.\n\nUsing advanced algorithms, we deliver a solution that prevents errors, avoids fraud, and optimizes fieldwork.\n\nContinue reading and understand how artificial intelligence is being applied in practice to modernize metering, protect revenue, and increase operational efficiency in the sanitation sector.\n\n### How does artificial intelligence contribute to preventing errors in meter reading?\n\nFor a long time, meter reading was a manual process, subject to human error, tampering, and constant rework.\n\nThis reality imposes operational challenges ranging from inconsistencies in billing to loss of trust from end users.\n\nTechnology, however, is changing this scenario.\n\nThe artificial intelligence applied by Jtech in meter reading review allows each measurement to be automatically analyzed in real time, based on historical consumption patterns.\n\nThis means that, upon identifying any significant deviation in the collected value, the system alerts the operator to the possibility of error or fraud.\n\nThus, the correction is made at the time of collection, eliminating the need for rebilling or revisits.\n\n### How does automated meter reading review with AI work?\n\nThe automated meter reading review developed by Jtech functions as an intelligent data validation system.\n\nThe algorithm uses machine learning to understand the individual consumption behavior of each customer, continuously adjusting to variations and evolutions in the historical data.\n\nWhen a new reading is recorded, the AI ​​compares it to previous data from that same consumption point.\n\nIf the variation is outside expected patterns, whether due to excess, scarcity, or anomaly, the system immediately signals an alert.\n\nAnother advantage is that the system learns from the corrections made. In other words, the more it is used, the more accurate it becomes, feeding on constant feedback that refines the predictive models.\n\nThis approach makes the solution increasingly adaptable to the reality of the operation and the behavior of users.\n\n### Benefits of artificial intelligence in metering\n\nBy automating data analysis, artificial intelligence makes the metering process faster, more accurate, and safer.\n\nThis reduces human error, improves decision-making, and increases confidence in the collected information.\n\nLearn now about the main benefits of this technology in sanitation.\n\n### Automatic identification of incorrect readings\n\nBy automating the analysis of readings, AI drastically reduces the incidence of errors before they even reach the billing system.\n\nThis prevents incorrect charges and administrative rework, as well as contributing to a more transparent customer experience.\n\n### Water Consumption Fraud Prevention\n\nArtificial intelligence also acts as a powerful ally in combating fraud.\n\nChanges in patterns that indicate possible improper tampering with the water meter, or behaviors inconsistent with the property's consumption history, are automatically detected by the algorithm.\n\nThis expands the power of oversight and ensures greater integrity in the process.\n\n## Increased Reliability and Traceability of Information\n\nData collection now has an additional layer of security and traceability.\n\nEach change is recorded, and all readings undergo a digitally validated process, which increases confidence in operational indicators and facilitates audits.\n\n## Less Rework and Rebilling\n\nBy detecting and correcting errors at the time of collection, our solution significantly reduces the need for rebilling, which is costly and exhausting for both teams and customers.\n\nThis improves the overall process flow and generates operational savings.\n\n### Jtech Solution's Differentiators\n\nWhat sets Jtech apart in the market is not just the application of artificial intelligence itself, but the complete ecosystem that integrates this technology into the reality of water utilities.\n\nThe automated meter reading review solution is based on cutting-edge technologies such as BigQuery, Vertex AI, and Pentaho, guaranteeing scalability, performance, and ease of integration with other platforms.\n\nIt is natively embedded in Sansys Water, Jtech's modular system that unifies metering, billing, and customer service operations.\n\nFurthermore, the solution communicates directly with Jtech's other operational modules, allowing information to flow in an integrated and efficient manner.\n\nMetering becomes a secure link between the field and the company's strategic data, supporting more precise decisions based on reliable information.\n\n## Intelligent Meter Reading: Efficiency and Control for the Future of Sanitation\n\nThe application of artificial intelligence to analyze consumption patterns within Sansys Water represents greater efficiency and control.\n\nBy automating meter reading review, Jtech not only eliminates errors and rework, but also strengthens the fight against fraud and increases confidence in operational data.\n\nThis intelligent approach transforms a historically vulnerable process into a point of operational excellence, aligning with the demands for efficiency, transparency, and control.\n\nFor utility companies, this means lower costs, greater credibility, and a higher quality service for the population, thanks to the application of artificial intelligence in the metering process.\n\n",
      },
